---
import PrimaryAction from "../components/PrimaryAction.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Product model — Auldric"
  description="How Auldric connects business sources, evidence, Marketing Strategy, go-to-market decisions, and reviewable next work."
  path="/product"
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Product model</p>
        <h1>Strategy that keeps its receipts.</h1>
        <p class="page-intro__lead">
          Auldric gives Marketing and Strategy work a visible chain from source material to evidence,
          decisions, outputs, and review.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="state-box">
        <span class="status-pill">Scope</span>
        <p>
          Auldric is focused on Marketing Strategy and go-to-market work. It is not a general coding
          or execution environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Source</p>
      <h2 id="source-title">Begin with what the business actually knows.</h2>
      <p>
        The workspace is designed around business sources: research, customer material, positioning,
        prior decisions, and other approved context. A source can support a claim; it does not become
        an instruction simply because it was imported.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Evidence</p>
      <h2 id="evidence-title">Make confidence inspectable.</h2>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Traceable</h3>
          <p>Material claims point back to their supporting source.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Qualified</h3>
          <p>Assumptions, gaps, and conflicts remain explicit rather than becoming false certainty.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h3>Reviewable</h3>
          <p>People can inspect a decision and its basis before approving what happens next.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="decision-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Decide</p>
      <h2 id="decision-title">Carry context into the output.</h2>
      <p>
        Auldric's Marketing Strategy and go-to-market workflows are designed to produce bounded,
        reviewable outputs. Decisions, unresolved questions, and the next work stay together so a
        handoff does not erase why a choice was made.
      </p>
      <div class="page-actions">
        <PrimaryAction />
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="/access">
          Read current availability <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
